    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245-a1">

                <pb facs="0523" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg453"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 625.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mitchell to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/>11. <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Abchurch Lane, King William
                                Street</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">London, E.
                            C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1883-09-20"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September</hi> 20,
                    1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inclose herewith a letter
                    addressed to this consulate-general by W. H. Russell, deputy governor in charge,
                    Millbank Prison, S. W., on the part of Michael or Patrick O’Donnell, who is
                    charged with the murder of J. Carey.</p>
                <p>The case presented by the letter is clearly one that does not fall within the
                    scope of the duties of his office, and is therefore most respectfully submitted
                    to you for consideration.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. H. MITCHELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Vice and Deputy
                            Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
